From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amaan Qureshi <git@amaanq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sched/fair: fix is_idle_core stub arity for !SCHED_SMT

The "Prefer the previous cpu for wakeup" prerequisite bundled into
cachyos/0012 declares is_idle_core(cpu, p) under CONFIG_SCHED_SMT and
every caller passes two arguments, but the !CONFIG_SCHED_SMT stub kept
the old single-argument form. CachyOS only ships SMT-enabled x86_64
configs so the breakage is invisible upstream; our mips (Octeon) and
any SMT-less config fail to compile. Match the stub to the SMT
version's !sched_smt_active() branch.

---
 kernel/sched/fair.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -7960,9 +7960,9 @@
 	return false;
 }
 
-static inline bool is_idle_core(int cpu)
+static inline bool is_idle_core(int cpu, struct task_struct *p)
 {
-	return (available_idle_cpu(cpu) || sched_idle_rq(cpu_rq(cpu)));
+	return choose_idle_cpu(cpu, p);
 }
 
 static inline int select_idle_core(struct task_struct *p, int core, struct cpumask *cpus, int *idle_cpu)
